From 47d3a2eae74a214c4898cc65e24a9acae2d1c5b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:21:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 830/831] perf(loader): ladder 64 KiB buddy sponge, allocate
 dense arena last, retain across drafter

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (series 0001..0829).
Upstream status: local candidate-63 patch for GB10 UMA boot-to-boot variance.
Quality implications: none; physical page placement and sponge lifetime only, zero numerical or graph changes.

Rationale:
1. select_buddy_sponge_target previously fell straight from 512 MiB (Order 13) to
   2 MiB (Order 5) whenever Order-13 free bytes dropped below required_bytes,
   leaving 2..16 MiB fragments unsoaked on aged 64 KiB nodes that still hold
   > 75 GiB in 32..512 MiB blocks. Walk descending 64 KiB orders (512 MiB down
   to 4 MiB) before falling back to 2 MiB..512 KiB; 4 KiB kernels keep their
   2 MiB hugepage ceiling unchanged.
2. bind_weight_arena previously allocated the permanent ~11 GiB dense weight
   arena (Q/KV/WO/shared/LM-head, streamed by tight L2 prefetch windows) before
   temporary pre-tile MoE storages, letting nvidia.ko's bottom-up buddy drain
   place leftover low-order fragments into the dense arena. Allocate temporary
   MoE storages first so the permanent dense arena claims top-order contiguous
   blocks.
3. BaseModelLoader.load_model released the target's buddy sponge before
   DraftModelSpeculator.load_model ran, forcing the drafter to re-soak newly
   freed low-order pages. Add hold_weight_arena_sponge / trim_held_weight_arena_sponges
   so GPUModelRunner.load_model retains (and headroom-trims to >= 16 GiB) the
   buddy sponge across target + drafter loading and releases once before KV
   allocation.

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py (50 passed).
